WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
At the factory, my mother often welcomed brothers who came to help.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
She treated them kindly and often gave them things.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
People wondered, “Why is she so good to them?”

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Then my mother gradually began sharing the gospel with them.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The Holy Spirit worked, and some knelt down to pray.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Many stories later unfolded in these people’s lives.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:57.000
One day, a Buddhist nun met my mother on the road.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Mother asked, “Would you like to go to paradise?” She said, “Yes.”

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Mother told her that those who believe in the Lord have hope.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Mother brought her to hear the gospel and told her not to be afraid.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:32.000
As she heard the gospel, her heart opened.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:43.000
She used to vomit when eating meat. That day she ate a rice dumpling with meat in the name of the Lord Jesus—and did not vomit.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Years later, when she was old and seriously ill, she no longer recognized people.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:04.000
When my mother visited, she asked, “Who are you?”

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Yet she still remembered that she had believed in Jesus.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:22.000
A single gospel tract became the beginning of salvation for our whole family.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:31.000
After my grandfather believed in the Lord, my mother apologized for not having loved him well.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:41.000
My grandfather was deeply moved. He said, “How could you say such a thing?”

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Mother hoped he would believe too. Later he did, and our family began meeting together.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:59.000
The story of my mother sharing the gospel is truly wonderful.
